title: I, the Unfortunate Daughter of India — The Nasrapur Rape Case
summary: >-
  Nasrapur rape case exposes systemic failure as a 65-year-old repeat offender
  assaults and murders a 3-year-old in Pune. Despite arrest, public outrage
  grows over repeated releases, weak justice, and rising rape cases in India,
  highlighting a cycle of crime, delayed courts, and society’s performative
  response demanding real accountability and justice.
